  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Paragon Systems obligated $351M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Paragon Systems won 215 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.6M. Obligations fell 41.3% year over year. Department of Homeland Security accounted for the bulk of FY2026 obligations with $286M, followed by Department of Health and Human Services with $38.4M and Department of Justice with $24.2M. Security Guards and Patrol Services is the largest market for Paragon Systems in FY2026 to date with $311M in obligations, and Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) follows with $40.1M. Historical obligations show peaks and troughs: FY21 $634M, FY22 $595M, FY23 $669M, FY24 $617M, FY25 $598M, and FY26 $351M. Current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year to date is still in progress. The figures here reflect contract obligations unless noted otherwise for award-value tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who buys from Paragon Systems in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $286M to Paragon Systems in FY2026 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $38.4M, and the Department of Justice obligated $24.2M. The National Archives and Records Administration obligated $1.2M, and the Department of Defense obligated $820K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets drive Paragon Systems' federal work?",
        "body": "Security Guards and Patrol Services accounted for $311M in obligations in FY2026 to date. Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) accounted for $40.1M. Those two markets together represent the declared NAICS markets for FY2026 to date."
      }
    ]
  },
